{
  "name": "Know who emails you: enrich new senders and flag decision makers in Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Know who emails you: enrich new senders and flag decision makers in Slack\n\n### How it works\nSpot the buyer in your inbox. The Gmail Trigger watches new mail that is not from your own domain and not a promotion. Each sender is handled once: Argorant looks up the person behind the address and returns name, title, seniority and company. Every match is logged in a sheet. Senders who are owners, founders, partners, C-level, VPs or directors are posted to Slack with the subject, so a decision maker never waits.\n\nCosts: 1 credit per sender found; misses are free.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Add a Gmail credential to **New email** and change -from:yourcompany.example in its search to your domain.\n4. Create a sheet with the columns date, email, name, title, company, seniority and pick it in **Log the sender**.\n5. Add a Slack credential and channel to **Flag a decision maker** and activate.\n\n### Customization\nAdd the sender to your CRM instead of a sheet, or skip free mail domains.",
        "height": 609,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "b7a2ff4f-6c87-4d87-a33c-2572ea2290a3",
